WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.120
I talk about the volume of pain.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:07.000
There are times
when it's so intense,

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.680
when the volume is so high,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.840
that I just wish
somebody would come along

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.680
and unzip my body
and just take it away.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.600
Humankind has constantly tried
to define pain.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.280
It isn't easy.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.440
- Most of the pains
that we feel are day-to-day.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.440
And they do resolve.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.880
They're part
of our body's protection -

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.160
making us rest and protect the area

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.960
and make sure it doesn't get
infected if it's a wound.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.360
And so day-to-day pain
may be kind of annoying,

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.760
but it is really important.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.880
A life without pain would be
very dangerous and life-threatening.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.760
- So if I were to tell you

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.080
how my pain is at the moment,

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.320
it actually feels today

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.200
as if someone has tried
to put a wetsuit on me.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.560
But this wetsuit is just covered
in tiny tacks

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.520
that are really, really sharp.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.720
And they're pulling
on this wetsuit all the time.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.760
It also feels
as if there are people with drills

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:29.960
on the soles of my feet,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.280
and there are lots and lots
and lots of people,

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.720
and they're just drilling
into my feet.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.040
And my legs feel really tight,

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.120
as if someone's got giant hands

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.640
that are just really,
really squeezing.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.640
- So neuropathic pain
is really intense.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.320
It's experienced
as almost real events,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:07.040
like being pinched and squeezed,

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.720
very severe,
what feel like electrical pulses.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:16.040
And clinical experts in pain
are able to right away identify

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.400
neuropathic pain
because of these awful descriptors.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.280
The last kind of pain,
the third kind of pain,

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.080
is really the mystery.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.040
And that is the existence of pain

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.280
for which
there is no obvious origin.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.800
So that does not in any way mean
that it isn't real.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.280
It's 100% real.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.520
It's just that our understanding
of our bodies is limited

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.760
at the moment,
and you can't find an injury.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.560
So, we're left with a population
of people who are really suffering

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.840
from pain,
and it interferes with their life,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.240
but we don't understand
where it comes from.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.760
- Pain itself
is a hidden disability.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.160
And I think it's really difficult
to get that across,

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.360
because you can't see
somebody else's pain.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.680
I suppose in every walk of life,
if you feel understood,

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:38.720
that's half the battle.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:44.960
And I think that journey
of trying to explain yourself

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.640
is a really hard one.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.280
It's absolutely exhausting.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:52.120
When you don't feel believed,

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.000
it has such a massive effect
on your mental wellbeing

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.600
that living with that pressure,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.680
it's almost just as hard
as the pain.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.320
And, well,
why should people understand

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.240
if they haven't experienced it?

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.640
But also
there is the word compassion,

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.880
and you're hoping that there might
be more compassion around.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:19.680
- I think the outstanding mystery

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.000
is why is it

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:26.920
that a substantial number
of our population

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:33.200
are suffering from pain without
any obvious biological purpose?

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.640
- I'm not sure that in my lifetime

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.600
there's going to be a magic potion

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.960
that suddenly will take
all the pain away.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.560
But I think the more
that we all talk about it,

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.000
that's where I feel hopeful.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.600
That's where
I can do my little bit.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.440
That's the optimistic bit.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.720
As for where all the nails
and the screwdrivers

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.680
and the drills in my feet will go,
I don't know.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:13.640
But I have to believe
that I will find my way forward.

